    <section><h2>An eight-step workflow for AI-assisted academic polishing</h2><ol><li><strong>Check what is permitted.</strong> Read assignment, syllabus, and programme rules; permissions and disclosure can differ by class and instructor.</li><li><strong>Decide what you can share.</strong> Do not enter confidential, unpublished, sensitive, or restricted material unless data terms and institutional rules clearly permit it.</li><li><strong>Set revision goal.</strong> Name highest-priority issue: thesis, evidence, paragraph flow, clarity, tone, grammar, or format.</li><li><strong>Fix argument first.</strong> Check main point, purpose, evidence, organization, and paragraph sequence.</li><li><strong>Inspect every suggestion.</strong> Keep, reject, or rewrite change only after comparing it with original sentence, intended meaning, discipline, reader, and voice.</li><li><strong>Protect facts and sources.</strong> Ensure revision has not changed result, overclaimed conclusion, invented detail, removed qualification, or weakened citation links.</li><li><strong>Finish sentence level.</strong> Check clarity, word choice, formality, grammar, punctuation, spelling, and format in context.</li><li><strong>Read as next reader.</strong> Recheck policy, privacy, thesis, evidence, source links, factual accuracy, voice, disclosure, and final submission responsibility.</li></ol></section>
